{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary","id":270617,"title":"We need a new Bygone Bestiary","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-01T22:35:15-07:00","id":270617,"title":"We need a new Bygone Bestiary","content":"Ok, let's face it. We desperately need a new Bygone Bestiary. Something for all of the creatures that could best be described as none of the above or relics of a bygone age that no longer matter. We need info on Dragons, both history and their modern day, we need new monsters, and info on how some could be living in your backyard without you even knowing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T21:46:48-07:00","id":272023,"title":"","content":"I play some D&amp;D. You know what books I have the most of? Monster Manuals. You know what makes for the most uninteresting games? Monster Manuals. What are games more interesting without? Monster Manuals. You know what I regret the most about my D&amp;D purchases? Monster Manuals. Lets not do more monster manuals for WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3870-tritium","name":"Tritium","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T04:47:37-07:00","id":272148,"title":"","content":"A new Bygone Bestiary doesn't need to be a Monster Manual. It may reflect how these creatures (non human, but mostly sentient, just as your average Garou) manage to survive, and wath role they play in modern world. For instance, we know that vampires have ties with mafia. Do dragons manipulate people too? or are they misanthropic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T10:00:08-07:00","id":272318,"title":"","content":"What's wrong with a Monster Manual? At all? It would be great to have some &quot;monsters&quot; around that didn't require almost completely stating out as NPCs. It doesn't all have to be about social interaction with peers. Sometimes the opposition can be a ghouled bear that is already stated our for me. It would be great a raven pooka who hangs out with other ravens, my Nosferatu who wants to use Animalism to have swarms of sewer rats at his beck and call, a Red Talon who wants to hunt beasties and hang out with other wolves, NOT having a nice set of staple 'things to fight', either stock NPCs or stock opponents has actually been a downside overall. Not that we need Monster Manuals I-VIII or Bestiaries I-V or the like, but ONE book sounds nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T10:54:12-07:00","id":272353,"title":"","content":"Oh, so many thoughts on this... I'll start at the top and work my way down.<br /> <br /> 1. 'Need' a new <i>Bygone Bestiary</i> is too strong of language as the NEED is not there, but it's a book that could use another look in the current classic World of Darkness (a bit of punning that I leave stand!). I'd think, though, we won't see such a thing until after the release of a 20th Anniversary Edition of <b>Changeling: the DREAMING* </b><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><b>NOT Changeling: <i>the Los</i>t</b></span>. Things like bygones and chimera and what-have-you seem to only apply to that game when discussed around books, even though <i>Bygone Bestiary</i> was ostensibly a supplement for <b>Mage: the Sorcerers Crusade</b>, but not exclusively so. Go figure that, hey?<br /> <br /> 2. The idea of a monster manual is NOT bad in-and-of itself, but really by the time of a <i>Monster Manual IX</i> offering the giant vampire dire shrew of Vecna for my <b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</b> campaign it gets, let's face it, bloody ridiculous.<br /> <br /> 3. I'd like to see a new version of <i>Bygone Bestiary</i> with a proper 'toolbox' ethic all the way throughout. I mean, there's some wonderful 'creature building' work in the original, but the chapter of monsters (the one that feels too close to a <i>Monster Manual</i> for my taste) doesn't offer quite enough in terms of possibilities. Further, the creation process in <i>Bygone Bestiary</i> feels very mechanical (again, a little too <b>D&amp;D</b> 'roll D100 on table of Monster Tail Features' for me), but I dunno if there's much of a way around that. Finally, I didn't like the conceit of these things as playable player characters; this is MUCH more of a 'mileage varies' sort of thing that any of the above, though, as some of us actually DO want that in the book. I'm just not one of them.<br /> <br /> ...All of the above notwithstanding, I think that <i>Bygone Bestiary</i> is a wonderful addition to the World of Darkness, and I'm glad to have it. That's something I cannot say about every book in my collection.<br /> <br /> <b>* Edit</b>: I know better!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":409,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","user":"Phaolan","date":".  I'm a dope! It's Changeling: the DREAMING! 10-05-2014, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T11:18:47-07:00","id":272379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=272353#post272353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. The idea of a monster manual is NOT bad in-and-of itself, but really by the time of a <i>Monster Manual IX</i> offering the giant vampire dire shrew of Vecna for my <b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</b> campaign it gets, let's face it, bloody ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. This is my problem with monster manuals.<br /> <br /> For the record, when you have a lot of monster manuals, you end up running campaigns that are, and I quote... &quot;Everyone ready? got your dice, your pencils, and soda... alright, round one, aarakocra&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3870-tritium","name":"Tritium","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T11:20:47-07:00","id":272382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=272353#post272353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 20th Anniversary Edition of <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Corrected that for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T21:27:40-07:00","id":272704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=272148#post272148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A new Bygone Bestiary doesn't need to be a Monster Manual. It may reflect how these creatures (non human, but mostly sentient, just as your average Garou) manage to survive, and wath role they play in modern world. For instance, we know that vampires have ties with mafia. Do dragons manipulate people too? or are they misanthropic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is kind of what I am thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T23:28:48-07:00","id":272776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=272148#post272148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...mostly sentient, just as your average Garou...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. Just, wow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T23:36:38-07:00","id":272778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=272148#post272148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A new Bygone Bestiary doesn't need to be a Monster Manual. It may reflect how these creatures (non human, but mostly sentient, just as your average Garou) manage to survive, and wath role they play in modern world. For instance, we know that vampires have ties with mafia. Do dragons manipulate people too? or are they misanthropic?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem here is that different game-lines view &quot;bygones&quot; differently. In WtA they are mostly Wyrm monsters that should be exterminated and are already covered in the &quot;Book of Wyrm&quot; in its various incarnations. In CtD they are &quot;chymere&quot; - critters made out of &quot;dreamstuff&quot; that, usually do not influence the real world.<br /> <br /> But in MtA bygones are real. The trouble here - they go &quot;poof&quot; (or &quot;splash&quot;) due to Unbelief and Paradox. Plus, they are &quot;thaumavores&quot; - i.e. they need to consume Quinessence regillarly just not to die in the real world. So, naturally, they tend to &quot;nest&quot; near Nodes. You know, a sought after sources of power by nearly every faction in MtA. Now try to imagine how much of them are still alive in the &quot;real world&quot; after the centuries of the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> There were a reason why early Tradition mages &quot;evacuated&quot; bygones to Umbral realms - to preserve them from the Unbelief. I see no reson for them to be any large presence in the modern WoD, barring the instances when a bunch of Marauders decides to bring them back &quot;to play&quot;.<br /> <br /> For me the original &quot;Bygone bestiary&quot; was totally useless. And I see absolutely no way how it's v. 2.0. would be any better. Ultimately, MtA is not a game of killing monsters and looting their corpses for Tass - at least, in my understanding. Surely, a new &quot;Book of Madness&quot; in its &quot;Marauders&quot; or &quot;Umbral Denizens&quot; chapter could cover some iconic creatures like griffins, dragons or unicorns. But nothing warrants an entire book about them. Maybe I do not see something here, then blame it on the fact that I'm totally unfamiliar with the tabletop DnD.<br /> <br /> As for the dragons - Aleph, have you seen &quot;Sin-Dragons&quot; from DA: Mage? Not a big loss, IMO. Actually, a chornicle set in M:TSC centered around slaying these monsters (ideally - by the Order of Reason group) is something I've been considering for some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","user":"von Lyttenburgh","date":". 02-01-2015, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T10:36:46-07:00"