class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=273257#post273257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm..maybe a write up on dragons would be better.<br /> Bygones Bestiary was kinda nice to read. But I get the feeling that a new edition could simply be a lot of material taken directly out of other books. And between that material and &quot;Beast; the Primordial&quot; it just might be redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly certain that the game plan for nWoD and cWoD is to make sure that they don't overlap and become redundant, and since B:tP is nWoD...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T15:36:03-07:00","id":273263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=273259#post273259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm fairly certain that the game plan for nWoD and cWoD is to make sure that they don't overlap and become redundant, and since B:tP is nWoD...</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... The core lines of [c|n]WoD overlap... some clarification on definitions would be required to justify that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3870-tritium","name":"Tritium","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T15:37:17-07:00","id":273264,"title":"","content":"I sometimes forget which forum I'm in...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T17:45:59-07:00","id":273342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tritium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=273263#post273263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh... The core lines of [c|n]WoD overlap... some clarification on definitions would be required to justify that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since when was there a core classic WoD book? There are multiple cores, which concentrate on playing a type of monster to the exclusion of all else. Little room is made for playing normal or normal-ish humans out of supplemental sourcebooks like Hunter's Hunted (II).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T21:54:58-07:00","id":274494,"title":"","content":"Read my post again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3870-tritium","name":"Tritium","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T22:40:02-07:00","id":274508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tritium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=274494#post274494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read my post again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apocalypse and Forsaken used to be stuck together awfully close. The present plan is to divide them to cover different territory, and this follows suit for other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T23:13:28-07:00","id":274517,"title":"","content":"Yes. Indeed. But your original comment was that a book covering one broad concept (which in the case of cWoD would be essentially a monster manual. My opinion on that still stands) could not happen due to there being a game line intended for player characters to play...vaguely similar characters as PCs. This does not hold. There are 2 werewolf games, 2 vampire games, 2 demon games, ....4 mummy games when it comes right down to it. There is immense overlap based on broad concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3870-tritium","name":"Tritium","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T19:57:22-08:00","id":361983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=272353#post272353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3. I'd like to see a new version of <i>Bygone Bestiary</i> with a proper 'toolbox' ethic all the way throughout. I mean, there's some wonderful 'creature building' work in the original, but the chapter of monsters (the one that feels too close to a <i>Monster Manual</i> for my taste) doesn't offer quite enough in terms of possibilities. Further, the creation process in <i>Bygone Bestiary</i> feels very mechanical (again, a little too <b>D&amp;D</b> 'roll D100 on table of Monster Tail Features' for me), but I dunno if there's much of a way around that. Finally, I didn't like the conceit of these things as playable player characters; this is MUCH more of a 'mileage varies' sort of thing that any of the above, though, as some of us actually DO want that in the book. I'm just not one of them.<br /> <br /> ...All of the above notwithstanding, I think that <i>Bygone Bestiary</i> is a wonderful addition to the World of Darkness, and I'm glad to have it. That's something I cannot say about every book in my collection.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>THIS!<br /> <br /> <br /> I think you've hit the nail on the head there Phaolan. We should remember that even though it was a bit of Mage, Changeling and Sorcerer supplement, it was of the World of Darkness Line. The books of that line suffered from not fitting neatly into any single system so sat in between many of them like inadvertent Crossover books. As such they seemed a bit confused in the organization and really specific in some aspects like talking about Mage Familiars, while being really Vague in others. (Water Zombies?... Really?)<br /> <br /> Much like your suggestion, I would really like to see a newer Bygone Bestiary handled more like a toolbox for porting creatures from either one game into another or from outside sources into your World of Darkness game, but even provide some guidelines on how to use these new creatures in every kind of game. It needs to be universal, not just for games with spirits or access to the Umbra. Bygones need their own little known back door to the physical world of reality. They need their own identity in the WoD not just as extras to come across or defeat if one is in the Umbra. Something not completely spirit and not quite classifiable. What I keep using as a resource instead of the Bygone Bestiary is the First Edition Storyteller's guide for Werewolf: the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> The first ST guide had sections with all kinds of fantastic ideas and creatures. From the Crazy Cat Lady, to the Jersey Devil. From Gaia's own version of Formori; the Kami, to the Wyld's own manic creations that really deserve attention as well. I use the closest template for the creature I'm using from Bygone Bestiary or from something from another system and use the ST guide for werewolf with some tweaks in order to use Bygone in my games. The Bestiary book itself does have some cool ideas and uses, but it really does deserve an update to the 20th anniversary world.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T09:24:03-08:00","id":401963,"title":"","content":"I just think we need Monster Manuel books of some sort that have lists for everything in a quick way for the ST to get their hands on. I don't want to go and look and buy a book I don't need just for some quick standard stats for the Local SWAT team if my Kindred do something the police would be involved in. Or my Werewolves are going deep in the Umbra and I have to find the exact page where some Bane Spirit is. Or where the hell are my variants on Hit Marks? What are the standard rules on an Earthbound Demon my twisted sick BSD wants to summon? What are Dragon stats for a Dark Ages game? or a Mage Game where you are in a Fantasy Horizon realm?<br /> <br /> What basic stats are there for a Professor, Street Walker, Serial Killer, the old lady down the block? What are some stats on elder Garou and Mages that I can quickly change and use? A stats on a BSD pack I can modify and change. <br /> <br /> How to level up monsters equal up to the creatures your Garou are facing. What are creatures that are equal too, higher than and lower than a Ran 2 Werewolf should be facing?<br /> <br /> I know. I know it is judgement calls and going through everything. I own as crap load of books. I love them but I hate trying to remember where a stat of a creature is in all the books I own. I want one reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T03:59:50-08:00","id":403176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=401963#post401963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think we need Monster Manuel books of some sort that have lists for everything in a quick way for the ST to get their hands on. I don't want to go and look and buy a book I don't need just for some quick standard stats for the Local SWAT team if my Kindred do something the police would be involved in. Or my Werewolves are going deep in the Umbra and I have to find the exact page where some Bane Spirit is. Or where the hell are my variants on Hit Marks? What are the standard rules on an Earthbound Demon my twisted sick BSD wants to summon? What are Dragon stats for a Dark Ages game? or a Mage Game where you are in a Fantasy Horizon realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are already such things as &quot;Antagonists templates&quot; in the back of each corebook. Each one. They are deemed &quot;enough&quot; for every more or less &quot;standard&quot; game. So, no - no Monster Manuals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=401963#post401963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What basic stats are there for a Professor, Street Walker, Serial Killer, the old lady down the block?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, c'mon! You can't write some stats for common humans personally?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=401963#post401963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to level up monsters equal up to the creatures your Garou are facing. What are creatures that are equal too, higher than and lower than a Ran 2 Werewolf should be facing?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't know - there are no level sistem in WoD. Each 2nd Rank Garou is different. It is quite possible to have 5/5/5 Physical Ahroun (1st Rank) Homid Fenrir and rather unimpressive in stats Lupus Theurge (4th Rank) Silent Strider.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=401963#post401963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know. I know it is judgement calls and going through everything. I own as crap load of books. I love them but I hate trying to remember where a stat of a creature is in all the books I own. I want one reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>One day I just wrote down in Word document all &quot;Medeival&quot; and &quot;M:tSC&quot; common human templates. So I don't have trouble to create, say, English Civil War Cavailer officer or a gang of beggars.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","user":"von Lyttenburgh","date":". 02-12-2015, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T10:56:38-08:00","id":403493,"title":"","content":"Using the term &quot;Monster Manual&quot; is apt to get a lot of perjoritive answers, even though, essentially that's EXACTLY what the Bygone Bestiary was. Including the &quot;how to make more of the same&quot; and &quot;how to use these critters in your game&quot; sections. <br /> <br /> Asking for more than the mostly random scattering and sometimes nonsensical templates in the backs of many many scattered books, doesn't sound like a bad request. Scion, which can't ever be accused of having a decent Bestiary (see &quot;nonsensical&quot; above, esp from the standpoint of them being decent antagonists for the characters), had a very concise set up of templates you could run as is for various &quot;levels&quot; of mortal (perfectly ordinary person, thuggish type, trained combatant, expert combatant) that was tremendously useful. It wasn't too hard to extrapolate them into similar vectors for improved social and improved mental normals as well. (Not that mortals are usually very important in Scion games and certainly not past a certain, very early point in the game.)<br /> <br /> If you don't have a decent place to get non-character-type opponents, you end up with a game where the characters are going to face mostly other critters of their particular type. Which is perfectly fine if you want that kind of game. It works well for a mostly social in-fighting vampire game. Most every opponent is going to be another vampire, even if it's a combat situation (combat is effectively &quot;aggressive diplomacy&quot; in such a setting). It works less well if you want to play a Mage game with spirits, space aliens, mythical creatures, angelic beings, the talking and dancing color blue, werewolves, etc. <br /> <br /> So I don't see why not to just have a Bestiary and other related books that give you things to interact with. Including some examples of Rank 2 Garou so you can run one on the fly if needed, either as is or with a few tweaks. Sometimes NPCs just happen. Ex. sometimes talking turns into fisticuffs and you don't have those stats ready for the character you though the PCs would just be talking to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T11:44:03-08:00","id":403519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=403176#post403176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are already such things as &quot;Antagonists templates&quot; in the back of each corebook. Each one. They are deemed &quot;enough&quot; for every more or less &quot;standard&quot; game. So, no - no Monster Manuals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, c'mon! You can't write some stats for common humans personally?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you don't know - there are no level sistem in WoD. Each 2nd Rank Garou is different. It is quite possible to have 5/5/5 Physical Ahroun (1st Rank) Homid Fenrir and rather unimpressive in stats Lupus Theurge (4th Rank) Silent Strider.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> One day I just wrote down in Word document all &quot;Medeival&quot; and &quot;M:tSC&quot; common human templates. So I don't have trouble to create, say, English Civil War Cavailer officer or a gang of beggars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seriously? The Antagonists don't cover enough. No I don't always have time to build everything from scratch. I want to easily get something together because I am a parent, I work and I want time with my family. Some quick generic stats like that just gives the Storyteller more time to design the game's story than just build every aspect of the system. It is the one thing many people have wanted for a bit. <br /> <br /> I have been running this game for 24 plus years. I know what the stats are. I said EQUIVELANT and how to raise and lower things for such a need. We don't have a massive list of everything we can need and use. Sometimes a reference book of NPCs and Baddies are needed for other games. It is something that cWoD lacks and something people have asked for for a very long time since the game started.<br /> <br /> There are times such when your players (as they should) throw a loop curve ball while running and you need to come up with a quick encounter you did not prepare for on the fly.<br /> <br /> I use to have a massive personal list of things I built. Then bang it is called a hardcrash drive I lost everything including my novel. I could not recover the data even had a company paid to do it and they could not do it. That was 15 years of heavy work from 1st edition to Revised. <br /> <br /> So yeah, a book with everything is great. Now more than ever. I like the idea of working on the story not just building all the time. <br /> <br /> The fact a Neonate, Ancillae, Elder or the RANKS 1-5 of a Garou bring in new encounters period. If I am playing a Rank 3 Garou things that I would face would be different than the Rank 1. I am not saying a level system. I am saying an equivlent here are a list of really big nasties or creatures you may not have considered to use based on the basic power structure. Let us not forget that Vampire, Werewolf, Mage for example have advanced creation rules to build more powerful creatures. <br /> <br /> Having am massive list of baddies and encounter with a book on how to build baddies and mystical creatures like Bygone all wrapped into one is a wonderful ST thing. Sometimes just seeing a reprint of a creature from another book that you have on your shelf will help spark an idea or set up for your group. Easier to modify and change than build from scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T12:48:47-08:00","id":403599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=403519#post403519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously? The Antagonists don't cover enough. No I don't always have time to build everything from scratch. I want to easily get something together because I am a parent, I work and I want time with my family. Some quick generic stats like that just gives the Storyteller more time to design the game's story than just build every aspect of the system. It is the one thing many people have wanted for a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what is your idea of &quot;enough&quot; for each gameline? Also, I can't really imagine a situation that you'd SUDDENLY need a stats for unicorn in, say, VTM game.<br /> <br /> Plus, there is no real need to stat just about everything. NWoD uses this sustem of describing non-Combatants only with dicepools in their most important skills.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=403519#post403519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been running this game for 24 plus years. I know what the stats are. I said EQUIVELANT and how to raise and lower things for such a need. We don't have a massive list of everything we can need and use. Sometimes a reference book of NPCs and Baddies are needed for other games. It is something that cWoD lacks and something people have asked for for a very long time since the game started.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again - I see no problem here. In MtAs 2nd ed there are examples for &quot;generic&quot; Mage PCs from Apprentice to Master. In some WtA book (Sotrytellers Handbook? Or was it ST Companion? Something Rev) there is this sidebar for creating High Rank NPC Garou. What prevents you from compiling them in a file for your future references? It's not that long or hard. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=403519#post403519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact a Neonate, Ancillae, Elder or the RANKS 1-5 of a Garou bring in new encounters period. If I am playing a Rank 3 Garou things that I would face would be different than the Rank 1. I am not saying a level system. I am saying an equivlent here are a list of really big nasties or creatures you may not have considered to use based on the basic power structure. Let us not forget that Vampire, Werewolf, Mage for example have advanced creation rules to build more powerful creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I'm not a DnD person (never played it, actually) so, I don't buy the whole &quot;encounter&quot; concept. Really, the age, Arete or Rank shouldn't influence the NPCs/Antagonists you encounter. 150 year old Toreador Ancilla has the same cahnce of encountering local gangbangers walking at night through a rough neighborhood as 13 Gen Neonate Malkavian. If your all-Cliath pack of Garous want some &quot;quick&quot; Glory and decides to go and pwn some Nexus Crawler - its their choice, not yours. Either they will succeed, or give them &quot;Darvin's Award&quot;. For the record - my players (4 Garou-strong pack) more or less did just that. But, because they were not (completely) stupid they've enilsted the help of the local spirits of the forest (hedgehogs and bunnies proved to be the most heroic of them), so, after several frenzies, near deaths and several Battle Scars they've PREVAILED. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/270617-we-need-a-new-bygone-bestiary?p=403519#post403519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having am massive list of baddies and encounter with a book on how to build baddies and mystical creatures like Bygone all wrapped into one is a wonderful ST thing. Sometimes just seeing a reprint of a creature from another book that you have on your shelf will help spark an idea or set up for your group. Easier to modify and change than build from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah-ha! And here I'm adressing the similar point raised for Ajax. For which game-line such &quot;Monster Manual&quot; will orient primarily? VtM and WtO don't need mythical critters. In WtO's case Plasmics are covered in 2 books, but it is perfectly possible to play a game without owning either of them. For WtA games there are various &quot;Books of...&quot; introducing new critters primarily as antagonists. And while Book of the Wyrm is, probably, as must have for any gamle of WtA, I can't say the same about others. Who else? DtF? MtR? No - they don't need critters. <br /> <br /> The only game that really uses Bygones as Bygones (and uses this name to reference them) is MtAs. New Book of Madness is already planned, which, undoubetedly, will include rules on Bygones and enough of their examples. Also, needless to say - you can play MtAs game perfectly well without Fish-Bishops or Harpies. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T13:48:55-08:00","id":403653,"title":"","content":"In a system like Storyteller... who the hell even cares? The only thing that's important is giving the character a reason to be there. After that point you just assign him a dicepool for stuff he does by thinking of the concept, without any care for his individual skills or attributes. If he's a critter just give him powers and describe them to look like critter powers, and use the same rule for their powers. The Spirits in Werewolf/Mage/KotE get this pretty damn well.<br /> <br /> It's simple, quick and lets you actually focus on what's important - the PC's and the plot.<br /> <br /> Also Von Lyttenburgh, can I just say that I really would have made the same statment as you did on who and why needed the Bestiary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T13:56:36-08:00","id":403672,"title":"","content":"I think there's not only a desire for something like this for each and every game, but a need for it. There is a reason why pretty much every game system out there has one. Even Amber could have used one. Actually, Amber could have used one BADLY, and that is an example of a game that takes the whole dichotomy of &quot;roll-playing&quot; vs. &quot;role-playing&quot; to it's nth degree. (A game near and dear to my heart and one I love beyond death in a wraithly fashion, but really, there is NOTHING out there but other people just like the PCs that have stats, if that). But I do agree Mage may need it more than the others. You can have a vampire game that is only about vampires and the game even encourages that to a degree, but it's not void of vampires vs. something other than vampires. I can see the relative merits of having them for various games as well. Werewolf seems like it would be a hair's breath behind Mage. A wraith game that wasn't Skinlands adjacent might have uses for it (critters of the Tempest, some specters stated out, etc.) And so on.<br /> <br /> PCs are massively unpredictable. I've had TONS of scenes where an NPC that was supposed to be scenery/chorus has fascinated a PC to the point that I needed some idea of rudimentary die pools. I've had NPCs that are made up for a particular purpose with just a set of rudimentary die pools that suddenly needed a much more complete write up (PCs that set out to go fight and then decide to talk, make friends, ask for services from what were planned as antagonists. There are more than a few times where scenery has made the jump all the way to full-blown interactive PC-level character at the drop of a hat. It's not like I haven't, can't and even am not currently winging that sort of thing, but, when running Scion recently, I discovered myself using those mortal templates a lot and I never have used the stat blocks provided in the various core and ancillary books in a similar fashion. In fact, every time I venture to use them, even roughly, they strike me as very unlikely. I would usually turn to someone like you, Von Lyt, to work through the analysis, but the stats they give for the various neonate/ancillae/elder, apprentice/adept/master, etc. just don't jibe at all with the relative power of PCs at those levels. And not in a &quot;PCs are awesomer than mere NPCs&quot; (if that's how you feel.... I can see it both ways, they are the protagonists, but that doesn't mean they HAVE to be Mr/Mrs. Special). They usually overpower PCs or just look really weird and not at all like what you would expect a character with # XP to look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 02-12-2015, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T15:43:32-08:00","id":403780,"title":"","content":"You know what's the best Monster Guidebook I've ever seen? Mythos Dossiers for The Laundry RPG. The book is 130ish pages. There is a grand total of 3 pages of stats in there. Everything else is just flavour, fluff, in character documents and props, logs and conversations between people and observations and scientific articles about strange monsters and stranger ideas. It's a glorious thing to read and it just bursts with ideas that you could use in any system and for all sorts of horrors. No wonder it got so many awards.<br /> <br /> If Onyx Path ever decides to do a monster book, it should learn from the popularity of Night Terrors and go full blown Mythos Dossiers on us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T15:51:05-08:00","id":403787,"title":"","content":"As much as a I enjoy all things Laundry (or Delta Green or most basic Call of Cthulhu), Mythos Dossiers is essentially fiction, like the original Vampire diary or Cathy's Diary by Sean Stewart. If you get 123 pages of fluff and 3 of crunch, it's not really much of a Bestiary at all. <br /> <br /> The Night Terrors books from the NWoD lines, came across more like a Bestiary, though, but it's very compartmentalized into specific channels. I'm not sure it's a lot different than having a bunch of really small adventures, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T13:35:26-08:00","id":405007,"title":"","content":"That's all you need for a bestiary. Night Terrors was too focused on giving things context so it can easily be fitted into bite sized adventures. That's the wrong approach. Get the storytellers and players imagination running. The point of a bestiary isn't the stats... it's to get your creative juices running. The best part of the Monster Manual are not the numbers, but the behavior, psychology and culture of the critters. That (and the art) is what you read the book like that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T20:21:45-08:00","id":407327,"title":"","content":"I happen to like the night horrors a lot &gt;.&gt;; A proper bestiary should have all that too. Culture, habits, habitats... ecology basically. Kinda like the earlier dnd monster manuals (i loved reading about the different kinds of dragons way back when). Probably why I like skin changers, predators, antagonists, wolfsbane, wicked dead and other such (hell i think i have the goblin market nighthorrors somewhere around here). <br /> <br /> One of my biggest irritation points about botw20th was the introduction of the Formarchs with no workable stats. What are their form stat bonuses for their shifted selves? Does unicorn maintain the same stats between human form and crazy ass neptune shark monster?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}